ding`,\nand the body on `body`. Use `2xl` for a page title, `xl` for a hero, `lg` for a section\ntitle, and `md` (the default) everywhere else."],[534,"`slot=\"title\"` inside a `Modal` or `Dialog` sets the accessible name."],[1970,"`sm` - Small spacing"],[46,"`Space` / `Enter`"],[1344,"`Space` toggles the switch when it has focus"],[1084,"`status` is independent of timeline and only controls the status icon and (for `error`) the accent bar color."],[44,"`Tab`"],[453,"`Tab`"],[482,"`Tab`"],[795,"`Tab`"],[855,"`Tab`"],[1565,"`Tab`"],[1391,"`Tab`: `data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focus-visible`, and `data-disabled`."],[1388,"`TabList` must be rendered inside `Tabs` and must provide `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. Give each `Tab` and its corresponding `TabPanel` the same `id`; React Aria uses that key to build their accessible relationship."],[1392,"`TabPanel`: `data-inert` when a force-mounted inactive panel is not interactive."],[1390,"`Tabs`: `data-design=\"underline\"` or `data-design=\"manilla\"`."],[1463,"`TextArea` is the multiline control inside a field, not a field on its own. Prefer `TextField` as the parent; see that component for fuller examples."],[1524,"`TextLockup` positions and type-sets its parts; you supply them. That means anything else can\nsit alongside them — a call to action, a second paragraph, an image — without the component\ngrowing a prop for it."],[1139,"`thumbNames` configures native form field names and does not provide accessible labels. Likewise, `valueLabel`, `minLabel`, and `maxLabel` are visual context rather than substitutes for accessible naming."],[831,"`titleInfo` requires `title` to be set — the info icon is contextually tied to the title label. If `title` is absent, `titleInfo` has no effect."],[1556,"`TooltipTrigger` wraps a focusable element and a `<Tooltip>`, handling hover/focus state and positioning automatically."],[1848,"`tooltipValueFormatter` shapes only the tooltip values, so you can show full